  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Southern Agriculture Growth Corridor Programme in Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To raise rural incomes and increase food security by contributing to the improvements in the business environment for commercial agriculture in Tanzania(especially the southern corridor), as well as growth in number and scale of commercial agribusinesses and substantial improvement in the market operations of a number of agricultural commodity markets. The programme is expected to benefit 100,000 rural households by March 2015 and over 230,000 households by end of the Programme in 2017</narrative>
  </description>
